// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// The radiance cache's filter (docs/render.md "Global illumination";
// ADR-0090, ADR-0091; gi_common.glsl): one invocation a slot, after the
// resolve. A cell's own mean is of the samples that reached it, and where
// little light arrives by few paths (shade lit by a sunlit wall across the
// street) a thousand samples leave it a tenth or more out, each cell its own
// way: shown as it is, the shade is mottled, and the mottling changes as the
// means wander. What the frame looks up is therefore each cell's light as
// its samples, its neighbours' and its parents' make it out together.
//
// The light a cell is held to have is the f that agrees best with its own
// mean m, by its samples' count n, with its six face neighbours' f, and with
// its parents' means P where its own samples are few:
//
//     f = (a m + b P + sum of g_j f_j) / (a + b + sum of g_j),   a = n / N
//
// the minimum of the cells' a (f - m)^2 plus the pairs' g (f - f_j)^2 (a
// Gaussian Markov random field's posterior mean; Rue & Held, "Gaussian
// Markov Random Fields", 2005), reached by one damped Jacobi step a frame
// (NPH_RENDER_GI_RELAX: the damping keeps the two halves of the lattice from
// swapping). The step's reach is 1 / sqrt(a + b) cells, over whose cells the
// samples' noise averages: N is the count that leaves the light
// NPH_RENDER_GI_SMOOTH_NOISE out, given how a sample spreads about the
// light (the variance guides the filter as in Schied et al.,
// "Spatiotemporal Variance-Guided Filtering", HPG 2017). So a cell whose
// samples agree keeps its own light and its detail, and one whose light
// arrives by few paths takes its neighbourhood's: from
// NPH_RENDER_GI_SMOOTH_REACH cells away at most (a + b is held to that). A
// cell that reaches further takes its light from where the light is another.
//
// The steps go from what each cell was held to be last frame
// (NphRenderGiView.held_before), not from its mean (ADR-0091). A mean of few
// samples moves by a tenth or more with each frame's, and a light that is
// held to be the mean plus what the filter added (as ADR-0090 first had it,
// to follow a change of the light within frames) moves with it, as do its
// neighbours'. While the camera stood still the means were of a thousand
// samples and the light held; at a run every cell near the camera is new,
// and the shade flickered by a fifth from one frame to the next. A cell's
// samples now move what it is held to be by a / (a + b + sum of g) a frame,
// their share of what is known of its light. Where the light itself changes
// the resolve sees it (ADR-0084) and moves what the cell is held to be with
// its mean, for those frames (gi_resolve.comp).
//
// Two things keep the filter from changing how bright the cells are
// together. A sample's spread is not the cell's own: where few paths carry
// the light a cell's variance follows its luck as its mean does, weights
// from it favour the cells no path has reached, and the shade came out half
// as bright as its samples' mean. It is the spread of the cell's parents'
// samples, pooled (below), the same for the cells around. And g is the same
// from either side of a pair.
//
// g is 1 unless the two cells' means differ by more than
// NPH_RENDER_GI_EDGE of their difference's deviation and
// NPH_RENDER_GI_EDGE_FLOOR of the brighter: then the difference is the
// light's own (the floor indoors against the ground outside a wall thinner
// than a cell) and the pair is cut loose. The deviation is the two cells'
// samples' pooled, from the variance the resolve keeps over the mean's own
// history (NphRenderGiView.moments' w).
//
// The parents (ADR-0091). Every sample is also added to the cells of the
// next NPH_RENDER_GI_ABOVE levels around its point (gi_update.comp): cells
// twice, four, eight and sixteen times as wide, which take four, sixteen, 64
// and 256 times the samples a frame, and whose histories are as many frames
// long (gi_resolve.comp). They give a cell three things:
//   - the nearest level's samples' spread and their light, pooled, which is
//     N's measure above and which the resolve tests a change of the cell's
//     light against (NphRenderGiView.cell_keys' z and w; a cell without
//     parents takes its own and its neighbours');
//   - P, their own means at the cell's centre, while the cell has fewer
//     than NPH_RENDER_GI_SETTLED samples: b is what it lacks of them, of
//     NPH_RENDER_GI_PARENT neighbours. Each level gives its means as far as
//     its cells' samples tell their light (NPH_RENDER_GI_PARENT_KNOWS of
//     them) and leaves the rest to the level above it. So a surface the
//     frame has just come to is lit at once, by the cells wide enough to
//     have had samples enough in a frame, smoothly and (their cells reaching
//     over what lies beside the surface) a tenth or so out; within frames
//     the levels nearer it know their light and take over, and then the
//     cell's own samples. Their means, not what the filter holds them to be:
//     a mean takes each frame's samples for what they are worth beside those
//     it has, where what is held moves slowly by design, and cells that
//     leant on it kept the light they began with for a second, a third too
//     bright. A cell cut loose from its parents as from a neighbour (their
//     light is another's) leans on them that much less;
//   - and through the last of its level's distances (from
//     NPH_RENDER_GI_BAND) what the frame looks up of the cell goes over from
//     its own light to what the nearest level's cells are held to be, to be
//     theirs where the level ends: the next level's cells begin there with
//     the same light, where the two levels' own estimates met at an edge
//     that followed the camera as a ring. (Over the whole level, as a
//     texture's levels are blended, the wider cells' light stayed in the
//     nearer ones for good: shade beside lit ground came out 3 to 15 % too
//     bright.)
// The parents are looked up in a cell's first frame and one frame in
// NPH_RENDER_GI_AROUND_FRAMES after (every frame while it is going over to
// them), and kept between (cell_keys' second vector).
//
// A cell in its first frame is held to be nothing yet: it begins with what
// its samples, its parents and its neighbours make it. Nothing counts for
// more than NPH_RENDER_GI_OUTLIER times the light around (one sample that
// met a lamp is a thousand times it). A cell no sample has reached for two
// frames steps one frame in NPH_RENDER_GI_AROUND_FRAMES, a workgroup's slots
// together, and from NPH_RENDER_GI_FILTER_AGE frames on keeps what it holds.
//
// arg0: the slot count. arg1: 0 leaves each cell its own mean (NphRenderView.gi_smooth).
#version 460
#include "vis_common.glsl"
#include "gi_common.glsl"

layout(local_size_x = 64) in;
layout(push_constant, scalar) uniform Push { NphVisPush pc; };

const vec3 k_lum = vec3(0.2126, 0.7152, 0.0722);
const ivec3 k_face[6] = ivec3[6](ivec3(-1, 0, 0), ivec3(1, 0, 0), ivec3(0, -1, 0), ivec3(0, 1, 0),
                                 ivec3(0, 0, -1), ivec3(0, 0, 1));

// The weight of a pair of cells whose means' luminances are `la` and `lb`, of `na` and `nb`
// samples whose variances are `va` and `vb`: 1 while the means lie within NPH_RENDER_GI_EDGE of
// their difference's deviation, falling away past it. The same from either side.
float pair_weight(float la, float na, float va, float lb, float nb, float vb)
{
    const float top = max(la, lb);
    const float pooled = max((na * va + nb * vb) / (na + nb),
                             NPH_RENDER_GI_SPREAD * NPH_RENDER_GI_SPREAD * top * top);
    const float floor_ = NPH_RENDER_GI_EDGE_FLOOR * top;
    const float d = la - lb;
    const float z2 = d * d / (pooled * (1.0 / na + 1.0 / nb) + floor_ * floor_ + 1e-30);
    const float edge2 = NPH_RENDER_GI_EDGE * NPH_RENDER_GI_EDGE;
    return z2 <= edge2 ? 1.0 : exp(1.0 - z2 / edge2);
}

// `light` (irradiance, and the far fields' luminance of it) held to at most `most` of luminance (no
// bound where `most` is 0).
vec4 at_most(vec4 light, float most)
{
    const float l = dot(light.rgb, k_lum);
    return most > 0.0 && l > most ? light * (most / l) : light;
}

void main()
{
    const uint i = gl_GlobalInvocationID.x;
    if (i >= pc.arg0) {
        return;
    }
    VisViewRef view = VisViewRef(pc.view);
    ViewRef rview = ViewRef(view.v.render_view);
    GiViewRef g = GiViewRef(rview.v.gi);
    if (GiKeysRef(g.g.keys).k[i] == 0u) {
        return; // free: the resolve left its entries zero
    }
    GiCellsRef raw_cells = GiCellsRef(g.g.raw_cells);
    GiHeldRef before = GiHeldRef(g.g.held_before);
    const uvec4 raw = raw_cells.c[i];
    const vec4 was = before.h[i];
    const bool smooth_ = pc.arg1 != 0u;
    const uint count = gi_word_count(raw.w);
    const uint age = gi_word_age(raw.w);
    // A workgroup's slots take a turn together one frame in NPH_RENDER_GI_AROUND_FRAMES (cells
    // that skip a turn in step skip the work with them).
    const bool turn = (((i >> 6u) + g.g.frame) & uint(NPH_RENDER_GI_AROUND_FRAMES - 1)) == 0u;
    if (age >= uint(NPH_RENDER_GI_FILTER_AGE) || (age >= 2u && !turn)) {
        // No sample has reached it for a while: it keeps what it was held to be, stepping with
        // its neighbours on its turns only while it is within the frame's sight.
        if (smooth_) {
            GiHeldRef(g.g.held).h[i] = was;
        } else {
            GiCellsRef(g.g.cells).c[i] = raw;
            GiHeldRef(g.g.held).h[i] = vec4(0.0);
        }
        return;
    }
    GiMomentsRef moments = GiMomentsRef(g.g.moments);
    const uvec4 mo = moments.m[i];
    const vec3 mean = uintBitsToFloat(raw.xyz);
    const float lum = dot(mean, k_lum);
    const float variance = uintBitsToFloat(mo.w);
    // Whether its samples have measured their variance: until they have, no difference is an edge.
    const bool measured = gi_moments_frames(mo.z) != 0u;
    // Its samples, as far as its history holds them (the word's count stops at its bits).
    const float history = float(gi_moments_history(mo.z));
    // Its light as the filter carries it: irradiance, and the far fields' luminance of it.
    const vec4 own = vec4(mean, gi_word_far_share(raw.w) * lum);
    // Held to be nothing yet: its first frame (or its light is none).
    const bool first = all(equal(was, vec4(0.0)));
    const bool known = count != 0u || !first;

    // The cell: its key's coordinates, level and octant (gi_cell_key), and what the filter keeps
    // beside it.
    GiCellKeysRef records = GiCellKeysRef(g.g.cell_keys);
    const uvec4 record = records.k[2u * i];
    const uvec4 kept = records.k[2u * i + 1u];
    const uvec2 kw = record.xy;
    const uint m17 = 0x1FFFFu;
    const ivec3 c = ivec3(uvec3(kw.x, (kw.x >> 17u) | (kw.y << 15u), kw.y >> 2u) & m17);
    const int level = int((kw.y >> 19u) & 31u);
    const uint octant = (kw.y >> 24u) & 7u;

    // Its parents: the eight cells of the next level around its centre. Their own means there
    // (`parent`, and how far it counts: `lean`), what they are held to be (`band`, for a cell
    // going over to it), and their samples pooled (`around`): looked up for a young cell, for
    // one going over, and for every cell one frame in NPH_RENDER_GI_AROUND_FRAMES, and kept
    // between (eight of the pass's fourteen lookups a cell).
    vec4 parent = vec4(0.0);
    vec4 band = vec4(0.0);
    float lean = 0.0;
    float going = 0.0;
    vec2 around = uintBitsToFloat(record.zw);
    if (level + 1 < NPH_RENDER_GI_LEVELS) {
        // The cell from the camera's (the key keeps 17 bits), and in the world's low 32 bits.
        const ivec3 camera = gi_camera_cell(g, level);
        const ivec3 rel = ((c - camera) << 15) >> 15;
        // How far through its level's distances the cell is: 0 where the level begins, 1 where
        // the next does.
        const vec4 origin = g.g.levels[level].origin;
        const float through = length((vec3(rel) + 0.5) * origin.w - origin.xyz) *
                                  exp2(float(NPH_RENDER_GI_LEVEL_BIAS - level)) -
                              1.0;
        going = clamp((through - NPH_RENDER_GI_BAND) / (1.0 - NPH_RENDER_GI_BAND), 0.0, 1.0);
        if (turn || first || kept.w == 0u || going > 0.0) {
            // The cell's centre in half cells: in the cells of the level `up` above, it lies
            // (2 full + 1) / 2^(up + 1) along each axis.
            const ivec3 centre = 2 * (camera + rel) + 1;
            float pool_n = 0.0;
            float pool_nv = 0.0;
            float pool_nl = 0.0;
            float parent_n = 0.0;
            float parent_v = 0.0;
            vec4 band_sum = vec4(0.0);
            float band_w = 0.0;
            // Each level above gives its cells' own means as far as their samples tell their
            // light (NPH_RENDER_GI_PARENT_KNOWS of them), and leaves the rest to the level above
            // it: where the surface is new to the frame its parents are as new as it is, and a
            // surface seen at a low angle has few samples in the nearest of them for long. The
            // nearer the level the less its cells reach over what is not the surface's (the
            // fourth level's, sixteen cells wide, held shade beside open ground a quarter too
            // bright), and the fewer their samples: so each as far as it knows. (A cell that
            // knows its own light leans on none: the nearest are enough, for their pooled
            // samples and for the cell going over to them.)
            vec4 gathered = vec4(0.0);
            float gathered_w = 0.0;
            float left = 1.0;
            float nearest = 0.0;
            const int top = history >= float(NPH_RENDER_GI_SETTLED)
                                ? 1
                                : min(NPH_RENDER_GI_ABOVE, NPH_RENDER_GI_LEVELS - 1 - level);
            for (int up = 1; up <= top; ++up) {
                const ivec3 v = centre - (1 << up);
                const ivec3 base = v >> (up + 1);
                const vec3 t = vec3(v & ((2 << up) - 1)) * (1.0 / float(2 << up));
                vec4 sum = vec4(0.0);
                float sum_w = 0.0;
                float sum_n = 0.0;
                float sum_v = 0.0;
                float there = 0.0;
                for (int q = 0; q < 8; ++q) {
                    const ivec3 o = ivec3(q & 1, (q >> 1) & 1, q >> 2);
                    const uint s = gi_find(g, gi_cell_key(base + o, level + up, octant));
                    if (s == GI_NONE) {
                        continue;
                    }
                    const uvec4 r = raw_cells.c[s];
                    const vec4 h = before.h[s];
                    const bool sampled = gi_word_count(r.w) != 0u;
                    const bool stepped = any(notEqual(h, vec4(0.0)));
                    if (!sampled && !stepped) {
                        continue;
                    }
                    const vec3 w3 = mix(1.0 - t, t, vec3(o));
                    const float cover = w3.x * w3.y * w3.z;
                    const vec3 e = uintBitsToFloat(r.xyz);
                    const float l = dot(e, k_lum);
                    const vec4 mean_ = vec4(e, gi_word_far_share(r.w) * l);
                    // Its samples, and how they spread: the nearest level's from their moments;
                    // the levels' above from their words, which count as far as matters here
                    // (and no spread: a cell is cut loose from none of those).
                    float samples = float(gi_word_count(r.w));
                    float spread = 0.0;
                    bool measures = false;
                    if (up == 1) {
                        const uvec4 m = moments.m[s];
                        samples = float(gi_moments_history(m.z));
                        spread = uintBitsToFloat(m.w);
                        measures = gi_moments_frames(m.z) != 0u;
                    }
                    const float knows =
                        max(min(samples * (1.0 / float(NPH_RENDER_GI_PARENT_KNOWS)), 1.0), 1e-3);
                    if (sampled) {
                        sum += cover * knows * mean_;
                        sum_w += cover * knows;
                        sum_n += cover * knows * samples;
                        sum_v += cover * knows * spread;
                        there += cover;
                    }
                    if (up == 1) {
                        // What it is held to be, or its own mean where the filter has not
                        // stepped it yet.
                        const float w = cover * (stepped ? 1.0 : knows);
                        band_sum += w * (stepped ? h : mean_);
                        band_w += w;
                        if (measures) {
                            pool_n += samples;
                            pool_nv += samples * spread;
                            pool_nl += samples * l;
                        }
                    }
                }
                // How far the cells that are there know their light, however many of the eight
                // they are: a surface seen at a low angle has had rays in few of its cells, and
                // one of them a cell's width away knows the surface's light better than all
                // eight of a level above.
                const float sure = there > 0.0 ? min(sum_w / there, 1.0) : 0.0;
                if (sum_w > 0.0) {
                    const float share = left * sure;
                    gathered += share * (sum / sum_w);
                    gathered_w += share;
                    left *= 1.0 - sure;
                    if (up == 1) {
                        nearest = share;
                        parent_n = sum_n / sum_w;
                        parent_v = sum_v / sum_w;
                    }
                }
                if (up == 1) {
                    // A sample's variance and the light around the cell, for the resolve's test
                    // of its light too (0, 0 while its parents have measured none).
                    around = pool_n > 0.0 ? vec2(pool_nv, pool_nl) / pool_n : vec2(0.0);
                    band = band_w > 0.0 ? band_sum / band_w : vec4(0.0);
                }
                if (left < 0.05) {
                    break;
                }
            }
            if (gathered_w > 0.0) {
                parent = gathered / gathered_w;
                lean = min(gathered_w, 1.0);
            }
            // Cut loose from them as from a neighbour, where its own samples say its light is
            // another (told against the nearest level's, where the light is mostly theirs).
            if (nearest >= 0.5 * gathered_w && measured && count != 0u && parent_n > 0.0 &&
                parent_v > 0.0) {
                lean *= pair_weight(lum, history, variance, dot(parent.rgb, k_lum), parent_n,
                                    parent_v);
            }
            // What the steps between find: the parents' light, the far fields' share of it and
            // how far it counts (12 bits each), over a mark that it was looked up.
            const float pl = dot(parent.rgb, k_lum);
            const uint share = pl > 0.0 ? uint(clamp(parent.w / pl, 0.0, 1.0) * 4095.0 + 0.5) : 0u;
            records.k[2u * i] = uvec4(kw, floatBitsToUint(around));
            records.k[2u * i + 1u] = uvec4(floatBitsToUint(parent.rgb),
                                           (share << 20u) | (uint(lean * 4095.0 + 0.5) << 8u) | 1u);
        } else {
            parent.rgb = uintBitsToFloat(kept.xyz);
            parent.w = float(kept.w >> 20u) * (1.0 / 4095.0) * dot(parent.rgb, k_lum);
            lean = float((kept.w >> 8u) & 0xFFFu) * (1.0 / 4095.0);
        }
    }
    if (!smooth_) {
        GiCellsRef(g.g.cells).c[i] = raw;
        GiHeldRef(g.g.held).h[i] = vec4(0.0);
        return;
    }
    const bool has_parent = any(notEqual(parent.rgb, vec3(0.0)));

    // What a cell's samples leave it with may be one path's light, a thousand times the light
    // around (a lamp met once): nothing here counts for more than NPH_RENDER_GI_OUTLIER times the
    // light around the cell, its parents' samples' pooled. (The cell's mean itself is kept: if
    // the light is the place's own, its neighbours' samples and its parents' come to say so.)
    // (Where the parents have measured none, the light around is the neighbours' as they are
    // held: below.)
    float most = NPH_RENDER_GI_OUTLIER * around.y;
    vec4 sum = vec4(0.0);
    float weight = 0.0;
    float beside_n = 0.0;
    float beside_nv = 0.0;
    float beside_nl = 0.0;
    for (int k = 0; k < 6; ++k) {
        const uint s = gi_find(g, gi_cell_key(c + k_face[k], level, octant));
        if (s == GI_NONE) {
            continue;
        }
        const uvec4 r = raw_cells.c[s];
        const vec4 h = before.h[s];
        const uint n = gi_word_count(r.w);
        const bool stepped = any(notEqual(h, vec4(0.0)));
        if (n == 0u && !stepped) {
            continue; // nothing known of it yet
        }
        const vec3 e = uintBitsToFloat(r.xyz);
        const float l = dot(e, k_lum);
        float w = 1.0;
        if (n != 0u && (measured || around.y <= 0.0)) {
            const uvec4 m = moments.m[s];
            if (gi_moments_frames(m.z) != 0u) {
                const float samples = float(gi_moments_history(m.z));
                if (measured) {
                    w = pair_weight(lum, history, variance, l, samples, uintBitsToFloat(m.w));
                }
                beside_n += samples;
                beside_nv += samples * uintBitsToFloat(m.w);
                beside_nl += samples * l;
            }
        }
        // (A neighbour in its first frame, which the filter has given nothing yet, knows what
        // its few samples do, and counts by them.)
        if (!stepped) {
            w *= min(float(n) * (1.0 / float(NPH_RENDER_GI_PARENT_SAMPLES)), 1.0);
        }
        sum += w * at_most(stepped ? h : vec4(e, gi_word_far_share(r.w) * l), most);
        weight += w;
    }
    if (around.y <= 0.0) {
        // A cell without parents that have measured their samples: its own and its neighbours',
        // pooled.
        if (measured) {
            beside_n += history;
            beside_nv += history * variance;
            beside_nl += history * lum;
        }
        if (beside_n > 0.0) {
            around = vec2(beside_nv, beside_nl) / beside_n;
            records.k[2u * i] = uvec4(kw, floatBitsToUint(around));
        }
    }
    if (most <= 0.0 && weight > 0.0) {
        most = NPH_RENDER_GI_OUTLIER * dot(sum.rgb, k_lum) / weight;
    }

    // How many samples its own mean counts as one neighbour for: as many as would leave the
    // light NPH_RENDER_GI_SMOOTH_NOISE out once the filter has spread them.
    float enough = NPH_RENDER_GI_SMOOTH_MOST;
    if (around.y > 0.0) {
        enough = clamp(around.x / (around.y * around.y) *
                           (1.0 / (4.0 * NPH_PI * NPH_RENDER_GI_SMOOTH_NOISE *
                                   NPH_RENDER_GI_SMOOTH_NOISE)),
                       NPH_RENDER_GI_SMOOTH_LEAST, NPH_RENDER_GI_SMOOTH_MOST);
    }
    // Its own mean by its samples; and its parents' for what its samples lack of
    // NPH_RENDER_GI_SETTLED, as NPH_RENDER_GI_PARENT neighbours at most and as far as they
    // count. Without parents its own mean never counts for less than leaves the step a reach of
    // NPH_RENDER_GI_SMOOTH_REACH cells, however its samples spread: a cell that takes its
    // light from further takes it from where the light is another. (Less while its samples
    // are a handful, one of which may be a path a thousand times the light: counted as a
    // settled cell's, it stood out as a white square.)
    const float by_samples = history / enough;
    const float b =
        has_parent ? lean * max(NPH_RENDER_GI_PARENT -
                                    history * (1.0 / float(NPH_RENDER_GI_SETTLED)),
                                0.0)
                   : 0.0;
    const float a =
        count == 0u
            ? 0.0
            : max(by_samples,
                  min(float(count) * (1.0 / float(NPH_RENDER_GI_PARENT_SAMPLES)), 1.0) /
                          (NPH_RENDER_GI_SMOOTH_REACH * NPH_RENDER_GI_SMOOTH_REACH) -
                      b);
    const float lent = weight + b;
    sum += a * at_most(own, most) + b * parent;
    weight += a + b;

    vec4 f = at_most(was, most);
    bool lit = known; // whether the cell is held to be anything
    if (weight > 1e-6) {
        const vec4 stepped = sum / weight;
        if (!first) {
            f = mix(f, stepped, NPH_RENDER_GI_RELAX);
        } else if (count != 0u || lent >= 0.25) {
            // Its first frame: what its samples, its parents and its neighbours make it. One
            // without a sample begins when a quarter of a neighbour's worth of them is there,
            // and is nothing until then (the pixels around it take the cells that are).
            f = stepped;
            lit = true;
        }
    }
    // What the frame looks up: through the last of its level's distances the cell goes over
    // from what it is held to be to what its parents are, and is theirs where the level ends
    // and the next level's cells begin, with that light. (What it is held to be stays its own
    // level's: its neighbours' steps take that.)
    vec4 shown = f;
    bool shows = lit;
    if (going > 0.0 && any(notEqual(band.rgb, vec3(0.0)))) {
        shown = lit ? mix(f, band, going) : band;
        shows = true;
    }
    // Trusted as its neighbours are where they lent it light (gi_surface_blend).
    const uint trusted =
        !shows ? 0u
               : (lent > 0.0 || going > 0.0 || count == 0u ? max(count, uint(NPH_RENDER_GI_TRUSTED))
                                                           : count);
    const float l = dot(shown.rgb, k_lum);
    const uint far = l > 0.0 ? uint(clamp(shown.w / l, 0.0, 1.0) * GI_FAR_ONE + 0.5) : 0u;
    GiCellsRef(g.g.cells).c[i] = uvec4(floatBitsToUint(shown.rgb), gi_word(trusted, age, far));
    GiHeldRef(g.g.held).h[i] = lit ? f : vec4(0.0);
}
